 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "In 1908, something flattened 80 million trees in Siberia.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.742
  },
  {
   "text": "Forty miles away, a trader felt like his shirt was on fire.",
   "s": 4.042,
   "e": 7.147
  },
  {
   "text": "Then a blast threw him clean off his porch.",
   "s": 7.447,
   "e": 9.32
  },
  {
   "text": "The explosion was hundreds of times stronger than Hiroshima.",
   "s": 9.62,
   "e": 12.626
  },
  {
   "text": "But nobody went to look for nineteen years.",
   "s": 12.926,
   "e": 14.873
  },
  {
   "text": "So what did the first expedition find?",
   "s": 15.173,
   "e": 17.014
  },
  {
   "text": "A ring of flattened forest, every trunk pointing away from the center.",
   "s": 17.434,
   "e": 20.93
  },
  {
   "text": "But at the center, the trees still stood. And there was no crater.",
   "s": 21.23,
   "e": 24.123
  },
  {
   "text": "Because the space rock exploded miles above the trees.",
   "s": 24.423,
   "e": 27.143
  }
 ],
